  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID TEKI Activity Fighting Plastic Bags With Sign Language</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TEKI is an Amharic word from the verb &quot;Metekat,&quot; which means replacing. TEKI Fighting Plastic Bags with Sign Language is a three-year activity funded by USAIDEthiopia and implemented by Teki Paper Bags PLC. The goal of the TEKI activity is to empower youths with disabilities to turn the fight against plastic bag pollution into a national employment-intensive inclusion solution.</narrative>
  </description>
